  "interpretation": "A conventional linear SVM under the identical nested subject protocol reaches 0.8054 independent balanced accuracy against the frozen decoder's 0.8317. The paired subject-level advantage of the frozen hierarchy is +0.0262 with 95% CI [+0.0107, +0.0426], reliable but modest, and the hierarchy loses on 21 of 62 subjects. The classic correlation/nearest-centroid classifier reaches 0.6964. These are the comparators the central claim requires, and they show the frozen result is well above the classic baseline and modestly above a modern linear one.",
  "note": "L2-penalised models are fitted in an exact dual basis spanning the outer training row space, which is mathematically equivalent to fitting all 13824 standardised features. Verified in tests/test_dual_basis_equivalence.py.",
