    "interpretation": "Removing the unlabeled subject-run centering drops independent accuracy to chance (0.2612-0.2883, tight subject-bootstrap intervals), a -0.52 effect roughly twenty times the frozen hierarchy's +0.026 advantage over a standard linear decoder. The centering step is the dominant methodological ingredient and is label-free but transductive. The balanced rule partially compensates (0.53-0.72) because forcing two events per class per run cancels the per-run offset that defeats argmax."
  },
